Ok, to solve this I used the gl2svdquartets function with method = 1, converted the nexus into individual population fasta files, and replaced all the "?" with "N". This all then goes in a folder that you can read into the PopGenome package.

On Thursday, 30 May 2019 12:12:22 UTC+10, Renee Catullo wrote:
> Hi Guys,
>
> I need to export fasta files with each individual represented by two rows, one with major alleles, and one with minor alleles. It needs to be nucleotides in order to use in the PopGenome R package, which only takes ATGCUN. Any suggestions?
>
> The names would probably be "ind_name_1/2_pop.
>
> Thanks,
>
> Renee

